# Committed template for media-proxy's storage credential.
#
#   cp media-proxy/.env-example media-proxy/.env-media-production
#   bash devops/minio/media-svcacct.sh production      # fills the two keys
#   bash devops/secrets.sh vprod media-proxy media-proxy/.env-media-production
#   kubectl rollout restart deployment/gbv-media-proxy -n vprod
#
# See documentation/secrets.md and planning/media-abstraction.md §4.3.
#
# Only the credential is secret. Everything else in config.go -- S3_ENDPOINT,
# S3_REGION, MEDIA_BUCKET, MEDIA_PREFIX, PORT -- is a plain value in
# devops/values/<env>.yaml. The key names below are exactly what config.go
# reads, which is why the secret is mounted with envFrom rather than remapped.
#
# NEVER COMMIT A REAL VALUE HERE. Written by devops/minio/media-svcacct.sh.

# The `media` bucket READ-ONLY service account: s3:GetObject on media/* and
# nothing else.
#
# Deliberately no s3:ListBucket. Asset URLs are unguessable capability URLs
# (§4.6); a list permission on the sole public read path would turn the bucket
# into a directory listing and undo the entire security model. It is also why
# there is no anonymous bucket policy at all -- MinIO's canned `download` policy
# grants ListBucket, and `public` grants write.
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
